Cytokinesis is the biological process where a cell physically divides its cytoplasm, organelles, and membrane to form two distinct daughter cells immediately following nuclear division.
The mechanism differs fundamentally between animal and plant cells due to the presence of a rigid cell wall in plants.
In animal cells, division occurs through the formation of a contractile ring. This structure is built from actin filaments and myosin II motor proteins assembled directly beneath the plasma membrane at the cell equator. Myosin and acti are formed due to Roah complex , which forms formins and rock .
Formins activates actin and rock activates myosin .Myosin motor proteins use energy from ATP hydrolysis to slide the actin filaments past one another, causing the ring to constrict.
This is similar to contraction of muscle. where myosin head is connected with actin. This action pulls the plasma membrane inward, forming a cleavage furrow that deepens until the bridge is severed 
